  "term": "Narcissistic Personality Inventory",
  "definition": "The Narcissistic Personality Inventory (NPI), in assessment, is a self-report scale widely used to assess narcissism, particularly its grandiose expression. As described in this source, it is based on DSM-III descriptions of narcissistic personality disorder and consists of 40 forced-choice dichotomous items in which respondents choose between a narcissistic and a nonnarcissistic statement.",
